WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.620
Beppy Columbo reached stable orbit around Mercury after an eight-year journey despite a shortened insertion burn. This is Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 263, web on Cassiopia A, a cosmic deep dive on stellar shell mergers and Euclid's distant quasar. Beppy Columbo, the joint European space agency, or ESA, and Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency, or JAXA, spacecraft, had a software issue that cut the insertion maneuver short.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.420
Separation of its two science orbiters is scheduled for December 9th.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.200
The mission will study the innermost planet's surface, magnetic field and exoplanet-like

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.360
environment in detail.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:46.620
Web's mid-infrared maps, in a Fizz.org report, show silica-rich dust in one reverse-shocked

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.660
ejectic clump of Cassiopia A, and carbon-rich dust in another.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:54.860
Cassiopia A is the leftover cloud from a star that exploded.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:01:01.040
The green monster region holds complex magnesium silicates left from mass loss before the explosion.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:08.160
The data indicate oxygen burning and carbon-burning shells in the progenitor combined only hours before the core collapsed.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:16.020
Lead author Tietemim of Columbia University said the merger can cause the shells to merge shortly before the supernova explosion,

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:20.180
and that it changes chemical abundances later found in the remnant.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:26.280
Co-author Dan Milisavlovich of Purdue University noted that resolving individual clumps at this

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:31.380
scale now ties the explosion back to the progenitors' makeup hundreds of years afterward.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:37.140
Massive stars stack their chemistry like onion skins. Hydrogen fuses at the center,

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:42.100
then helium, carbon, oxygen, and heavier elements burn in shells stacked outward.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:47.980
Gravity holds the layers apart until the stars last hours. When those oxygen burning and

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:53.160
carbon-burning shells combine, matter from different nuclear processes mixes, and the interior

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:53.900
is rewritten.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.440
How often such mergers happen among stars that collapse, and whether the abundance patterns

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.800
show up in the spectra of distant supernovae remains unknown.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:08.040
A larger set of young remnants seen at similar mid-infrared resolution would settle it.

00:02:09.038 --> 00:02:14.698
Euclid's wide survey, ESA reported, first flagged an object that follow up with multiple ground

00:02:14.698 --> 00:02:19.058
and space-based telescopes confirmed as the most distant quasar found to date.

00:02:19.598 --> 00:02:24.778
A quasar is a galaxy's bright core, powered by a black hole feeding on surrounding gas.

00:02:25.498 --> 00:02:28.818
The fine tightens limits on models of early black hole formation.

